[metadata] {"type": "create", "filePath": "/app/output/final_report.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Student Performance Analytics Report: Bangladesh</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js"></script>
    <style>
        :root {
            --primary: #1a365d;
            --secondary: #2c5282;
            --accent: #3182ce;
            --success: #38a169;
            --warning: #d69e2e;
            --danger: #e53e3e;
            --bg: #f7fafc;
            --card-bg: #ffffff;
            --text: #1a202c;
            --text-muted: #718096;
            --border: #e2e8f0;
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
        body {
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .container { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
        header {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
            color: white;
            padding: 40px 20px;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }
        header h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
        header p { opacity: 0.9; font-size: 1.1rem; }
        .meta { display: flex; gap: 20px; font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.8; margin-top: 10px; }
        h2 { color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 30px 0 15px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); }
        h3 { color: var(--secondary); font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 20px 0 10px; }
        .kpi-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
            gap: 15px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .kpi-card {
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 20px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
        }
        .kpi-card.success { border-left-color: var(--success); }
        .kpi-card.warning { border-left-color: var(--warning); }
        .kpi-card.danger { border-left-color: var(--danger); }
        .kpi-label { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
        .kpi-value { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin: 5px 0; }
        .kpi-sub { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
        .indicator { display: inline-block; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 5px; }
        .indicator.green { background: var(--success); }
        .indicator.yellow { background: var(--warning); }
        .indicator.red { background: var(--danger); }
        .card {
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 24px;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .stat-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 30px; margin: 15px 0; }
        .stat-item { min-width: 120px; }
        .stat-label { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
        .stat-value { font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--primary); }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 15px 0; }
        th, td { padding: 12px 15px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
        th { background: var(--bg); font-weight: 600; color: var(--primary); }
        tr:hover { background: var(--bg); }
        .highlight-box {
            background: #ebf8ff;
            border: 1px solid var(--accent);
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .highlight-box.warning {
            background: #fefce8;
            border-color: var(--warning);
        }
        .highlight-box.success {
            background: #f0fff4;
            border-color: var(--success);
        }
        .chart-container { position: relative; height: 350px; margin: 20px 0; }
        .grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(450px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; }
        .recommendation {
            background: var(--card-bg);
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
            box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
        }
        .recommendation h4 { color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 8px; }
        .recommendation p { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; }
        .tag {
            display: inline-block;
            padding: 3px 10px;
            border-radius: 20px;
            font-size: 0.75rem;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
        .tag-success { background: #c6f6d5; color: #22543d; }
        .tag-warning { background: #fefcbf; color: #744210; }
        .tag-neutral { background: #e2e8f0; color: #4a5568; }
        .callout {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ebf8ff, #e6fffa);
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 20px 0;
            border: 1px solid #81e6d9;
        }
        .callout-title { font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 8px; }
        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 30px;
            color: var(--text-muted);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            margin-top: 40px;
        }
        .exec-summary {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--primary), var(--secondary));
            color: white;
            border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 30px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .exec-summary h2 { color: white; border-bottom-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.3); }
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
            .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <div class="container">
            <h1>Student Performance Analytics Report: Bangladesh</h1>
            <p>Factors Influencing Academic Outcomes Across Districts</p>
            <div class="meta">
                <span>Report Date: May 2026</span>
                <span>Dataset: 1,000 Students | 8 Districts | 14 Variables</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
        <!-- EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
        <div class="exec-summary">
            <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
            <p>This analysis of 1,000 students across 8 Bangladeshi districts reveals a student population performing at a <strong>mean HSC GPA of 4.01</strong> (scale 0–5). Performance is remarkably uniform across demographic segments — gender, school type, income quartiles, and parent education levels all show statistically insignificant effect sizes on HSC outcomes. The most actionable finding is the <strong>SSC-to-HSC performance decline</strong> (average −0.24 GPA points), which represents a system-level pattern of academic regression between examination cycles. Regional disparities, while real (Barisal highest at 4.11, Rangpur lowest at 3.91), are modest in magnitude relative to within-district variation.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- KPIs -->
        <h2>Key Performance Indicators</h2>
        <div class="kpi-grid">
            <div class="kpi-card">
                <div class="kpi-label">Average HSC Result</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">4.01</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub"><span class="indicator green"></span>On a 0–5 scale</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card success">
                <div class="kpi-label">Excellent Performance Rate</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">26.8%</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub">268 of 1,000 students achieved GPA ≥ 4.5</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card success">
                <div class="kpi-label">At-Risk Student Rate</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">0.0%</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub"><span class="indicator green"></span>No students below 3.0 GPA</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card warning">
                <div class="kpi-label">GPA Progression Delta</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">+0.02</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub">HSC minus Previous GPA (marginal improvement)</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kpi-card">
                <div class="kpi-label">Attendance-Performance Correlation</div>
                <div class="kpi-value">−0.01</div>
                <div class="kpi-sub"><span class="indicator yellow"></span>No meaningful correlation</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- DEMOGRAPHIC OVERVIEW -->
        <h2>Student Demographic Overview</h2>
        <div class="card">
            <p>The dataset comprises 1,000 students distributed across 8 districts, with balanced representation by gender (51% Female, 49% Male) and school type (52.4% Private, 47.6% Public). Student ages range from 15 to 18 years with a mean of 16.4 years. Parent education distribution is relatively even, with Graduates representing the largest segment (26.7%), followed by Higher Secondary (25.1%), Secondary (24.7%), and Primary (23.5%). Internet access at home is available to 47.8% of students, while 50.3% receive private tuition.</p>

            <div class="grid-2">
                <div>
                    <h3>District Distribution</h3>
                    <table>
                        <tr><th>District</th><th>Students</th><th>Share</th></tr>
                        <tr><td>Chattogram</td><td>133</td><td>13.3%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Khulna</td><td>131</td><td>13.1%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Dhaka</td><td>130</td><td>13.0%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Barisal</td><td>125</td><td>12.5%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Rangpur</td><td>123</td><td>12.3%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Rajshahi</td><td>122</td><td>12.2%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Mymensingh</td><td>119</td><td>11.9%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Sylhet</td><td>117</td><td>11.7%</td></tr>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Gender & School Type</h3>
                    <table>
                        <tr><th>Category</th><th>Count</th><th>Percentage</th></tr>
                        <tr><td>Female</td><td>510</td><td>51.0%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Male</td><td>490</td><td>49.0%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Private School</td><td>524</td><td>52.4%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Public School</td><td>476</td><td>47.6%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Private Tuition: Yes</td><td>503</td><td>50.3%</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Internet Access: Yes</td><td>478</td><td>47.8%</td></tr>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS -->
        <h2>Academic Performance Analysis</h2>
        <div class="card">
            <p>Three GPA measurements capture academic progression: <strong>Previous GPA</strong> (mean 3.995), <strong>SSC Result</strong> (mean 4.257), and <strong>HSC Result</strong> (mean 4.013). The critical finding is the performance trajectory from SSC to HSC: students average a <strong>−0.24 decline</strong> between these two examinations, despite a +0.02 improvement from Previous GPA to HSC. This suggests the HSC examination introduces significant regression relative to SSC performance that is not present in the earlier-to-SSC trajectory.</p>

            <div class="stat-row">
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <div class="stat-label">Previous GPA Mean</div>
                    <div class="stat-value">3.995</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <div class="stat-label">SSC Result Mean</div>
                    <div class="stat-value">4.257</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <div class="stat-label">HSC Result Mean</div>
                    <div class="stat-value">4.013</div>
                </div>
                <div class="stat-item">
                    <div class="stat-label">Pass Rate (≥2.0)</div>
                    <div class="stat-value">100%</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Performance Classification (HSC Results)</h3>
            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="performanceChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <div class="highlight-box warning">
                <strong>Key Observation:</strong> No students scored below 3.0 GPA on the HSC (At-Risk Rate = 0%), but 49.4% of students fall in the "Average" category (3.0–3.99). The largest single classification is "Average" at 49.4%, indicating broad middle-ground performance with limited students achieving "Good" (23.8%) or "Excellent" (26.8%) status.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SOCIOECONOMIC IMPACT -->
        <h2>Socio-Economic Factors and Their Impact on Performance</h2>
        <div class="card">
            <div class="callout">
                <div class="callout-title">Critical Finding: Socio-Economic Factors Show Minimal Impact on HSC Outcomes</div>
                <p>Contrary to typical patterns in educational research, this dataset reveals <strong>near-zero effect sizes</strong> for income, parent education, and internet access on HSC performance. All correlations are statistically non-significant (p > 0.05), and Cohen's d effect sizes are negligible (all < 0.10). This suggests other factors may dominate student outcomes in this dataset, or the sampled population is relatively homogenous in socio-economic terms.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="grid-2">
                <div>
                    <h3>Family Income vs. HSC Result</h3>
                    <p>Income-HSC correlation: <strong>r = −0.007</strong> (essentially zero)</p>
                    <table>
                        <tr><th>Income Quartile</th><th>Mean HSC</th><th>Std Dev</th></tr>
                        <tr><td>Q1 (Lowest)</td><td>4.023</td><td>0.597</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Q2</td><td>3.992</td><td>0.590</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Q3</td><td>4.025</td><td>0.581</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Q4 (Highest)</td><td>4.012</td><td>0.592</td></tr>
                    </table>
                    <p style="margin-top:10px; font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Mean income range: 33,694–36,650 BDT/month. The income spread across quartiles is relatively narrow, which may explain the lack of performance variation.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Parent Education vs. HSC Result</h3>
                    <p>Effect size (Graduate vs. Primary): <strong>Cohen's d = 0.063</strong> (negligible)</p>
                    <table>
                        <tr><th>Parent Education</th><th>Mean HSC</th><th>Std Dev</th></tr>
                        <tr><td>Primary</td><td>3.964</td><td>0.591</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Graduate</td><td>4.001</td><td>0.583</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Higher Secondary</td><td>4.035</td><td>0.595</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Secondary</td><td>4.050</td><td>0.589</td></tr>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Internet Access Impact</h3>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Internet Access</th><th>Students</th><th>Mean HSC</th><th>Effect Size (Cohen's d)</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Yes</td><td>478</td><td>4.022</td><td rowspan="2">0.029 (negligible)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>No</td><td>522</td><td>4.004</td></tr>
            </table>
            <p style="margin-top:10px; font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--text-muted);">p-value = 0.647 (not statistically significant)</p>

            <h3>Private Tuition Impact</h3>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Private Tuition</th><th>Students</th><th>Mean HSC</th><th>p-value</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Yes</td><td>503</td><td>4.019</td><td rowspan="2">0.746 (not significant)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>No</td><td>497</td><td>4.007</td></tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <!-- STUDY BEHAVIOR AND ATTENDANCE -->
        <h2>Study Behavior and Attendance Patterns</h2>
        <div class="card">
            <p>Study hours per week (mean 16.7 hours, range 5–29) show no meaningful correlation with HSC results (r = −0.022). Similarly, attendance rates (mean 79.5%, range 60–99%) have essentially zero correlation with HSC performance (r = −0.014). This counter-intuitive finding may reflect a threshold effect: once a minimum level of study and attendance is reached, additional effort does not translate to measurably better HSC outcomes in this dataset.</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <canvas id="studyChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>Study Hours vs. Performance</h3>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Study Hours/Week</th><th>Students</th><th>Mean HSC</th></tr>
                <tr><td>1–10 hours</td><td>245</td><td>4.034</td></tr>
                <tr><td>11–20 hours</td><td>378</td><td>3.986</td></tr>
                <tr><td>21–30 hours</td><td>377</td><td>4.025</td></tr>
            </table>

            <h3>Attendance Quartiles vs. Performance</h3>
            <table>
                <tr><th>Attendance Level</th><th>Mean HSC</th></tr>
                <tr><td>Low (Q1)</td><td>4.017</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Medium-Low (Q2)</td><td>3.997</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Medium-High (Q3)</td><td>4.082</td></tr>
                <tr><td>High (Q4)</td><td>3.948</td></tr>
            </table>

            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Interpretation:</strong> Neither study hours nor attendance percentage predict HSC performance in this dataset. This suggests the quality and effectiveness of study time may matter more than raw quantity, and that attendance policies alone are insufficient levers for improving examination outcomes.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- REGIONAL DISPARITIES -->
        <h2>Regional Performance Disparities</h2>
        <div class="card">
            <p>District-level HSC performance ranges from 3.91 to 4.11, a spread of 0.20 GPA points. While statistically significant (F-test p < 0.05), this 0.20-point range represents only about one-third of a standard deviation (σ = 0.59), suggesting limited practical significance. Barisal leads performance, while Rangpur trails, but the magnitude of difference is modest compared to within-district variance.</p>

            <div class="chart-container" style="height:400px;">
                <canvas id="districtChart"></canvas>
            </div>

            <h3>District Rankings by Mean HSC Result</h3>
            <table>
